# The driver plugin directory: the one place a driver jar goes on this machine, read by bootRun,
# :command-deck:driverPluginTest and script/run-bench.ps1 alike. Neither jar belongs in git -
# dscusb is published to GitHub Packages, usbmodbus is licence-restricted - and a tracked copy
# silently diverging from the sibling repo it is built from is worse than no copy.
#
# The jars, not the directory: its README is tracked so a fresh clone still shows what belongs
# there, the same arrangement as docker/drivers-local/ below.
#
# Anchored deliberately. Unanchored it once swallowed command-deck/src/drivers/ (a vendor-adapter
# source set that no longer exists), whose files then never showed up in git status at all. Keep it
# anchored so a future directory named drivers/ anywhere else does not vanish the same way.
/drivers/*.jar
# Error screenshots generated by TestBench for failed integration tests
error-screenshots/
webpack.generated.js

frontend/themes/hilla-react-app/theme-editor.css

.fleet/

script/.data
scrtip/app.log

/.secrets
# Local-only deployment secrets: PKCS12 keystore holds an SSL private key
docker/keystore/
docker/.secrets/
# Per-host compose config. Carries KEY_STORE_PASSWORD, so it is a credential file however harmless
# the default looks. Copy docker/.env.example, which is tracked and holds the non-secret defaults.
docker/.env
# Database dump taken from a live instance
docker/backup.sql

# Runtime settings written by SettingRepository in dev
/settings.json
*/settings.json
!.claude/settings.json

*.bak

# Classes extracted from drivers/usbmodbus.jar during investigation. That jar's
# committed either.
umb/

# supervisord logs and perms dumps from container runs
docker/test/